          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तूलिका — tūlikā — \"a paintbrush\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चित्रकारः नूतनां तूलिकां क्रीणाति। citrakāraḥ nūtanāṃ tūlikāṃ krīṇāti. The painter buys a new brush."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तूलिका (tūlikā) is the word MW gives as the same as tūli, a painter's brush; MW gives no further derivation, so its origin is uncertain (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
